  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "On the avatar I'm making I have it setup to have multiple UV maps on a poiyomi shader that are swapped in-between  to act as multiple texture states. When I use a puppet menu that is used for facial expression it it swaps the texture if not on the default to the previous state or to default sometimes after a few UV swaps it will flicker to the second UV. ive checked over my animations and have found no issues in animations triggering the uv swap or with the FX layer not being set up properly they work in blender and the two systems are relatively separate for being in the same controller file and they don't even do anything that would affect each other one drives blendshapes the other drives a specific value. hopefully if this is a bug it is fixed quickly cuase multiple meshes is dumb and really can be done differently and more performantly with shader changes and blend shapes and its not that hard. anyways happy chatting out there hopefully a workaround is found to this bug or its fixed because I would love to se the magic of 3.0 unhindered by bugs blocking us from doing more performant things with our avatars.",
